---
import BaseLayout from "@layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "Copyright + Licensing";
const description =
  "What is ours, what is not, how to reuse it, and how to send a copyright notice — the licensing and takedown policy for The Dictionary of Color Combinations.";

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "WebPage",
  name: title,
  description,
  url: new URL("/copyright/", Astro.site).toString(),
  isPartOf: {
    "@type": "WebSite",
    name: "The Dictionary of Color Combinations",
    url: Astro.site?.toString(),
  },
};
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <article class="legal-page section">
    <div class="container-prose">
      <header class="legal-page__header">
        <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
        <h1>Copyright + Licensing</h1>
        <p class="legal-page__updated">Last updated: September 2026</p>
      </header>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          This archive sits on top of a public-domain historical work, so it is worth being
          precise about which layer is whose. The short version: the colours and their names
          are facts and free; our compositions, writing, and curation are ours and are given
          away under a permissive licence; the digitisation layer belongs to someone else and
          is credited. The full method is documented on the
          <a href="/methodology/">methodology page</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>What is ours</h2>
        <p>
          The following are original work of The Dictionary of Color Combinations
          (<strong>colorcombinations.org</strong>), published by
          <a href="https://caslonmedia.com/" rel="publisher">Caslon Media</a>:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>The 30 editorial palette compositions</strong> — original combinations built
            with Wada's method, not reproductions of his plates.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Editorial writing</strong> — palette descriptions, colour meanings, usage
            guidance, collection essays, and the learn/reference articles.
          </li>
          <li><strong>Curation and structure</strong> — the collections, tagging, and site architecture.</li>
          <li><strong>Design and code</strong> — layout, typography, components, and the tools.</li>
          <li>
            <strong>Generated imagery</strong> — the social and Pinterest cards rendered by this
            site for each page.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          All of it is released under
          <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CC BY 4.0</a>.
          You may copy, adapt, and use it commercially, including for machine-learning training,
          provided you credit <strong>colorcombinations.org</strong>. A link back is the simplest
          way to do that.
        </p>

        <h2>What is not ours</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>The 348 historical plates.</strong> Sanzo Wada's <em>A Dictionary of Color
            Combinations</em> (1933, six volumes) is in the public domain by age. We claim no
            rights over it.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Colour names and hex values are facts.</strong> A colour and its name cannot
            be owned. Use them freely, from us or from anywhere else.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>The digitisation layer belongs to its author.</strong> Our plate data derives
            from
            <a href="https://github.com/mattdesl/dictionary-of-colour-combinations" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">mattdesl/dictionary-of-colour-combinations</a>,
            which is MIT-licensed. If you reuse the plate data, carry that credit: this site for
            the curation, <strong>mattdesl</strong> for the digitisation, and <strong>Sanzo
            Wada</strong> for the original work.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Book covers and product images</strong> shown beside recommendation and
            affiliate links identify the item being linked and remain the property of their
            respective publishers and rights-holders.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Paintings.</strong> Works in the painting palettes are public-domain pieces;
            each entry records its licence status and its sources on the page itself.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Trademarks</h2>
        <p>
          "A Dictionary of Color Combinations" is the title of Sanzo Wada's work as reprinted by
          Seigensha Art Publishing (2010). This site is an independent reference project and is
          not affiliated with, endorsed by, or connected to Seigensha Art Publishing or the Wada
          estate. Other product and company names mentioned are the marks of their respective
          owners.
        </p>

        <h2>Notice and takedown</h2>
        <p>
          If you believe material on this site infringes your copyright, email
          <a href="mailto:hello@caslonmedia.com?subject=Copyright+notice">hello@caslonmedia.com</a>
          with the subject line <strong>"Copyright notice"</strong> and include:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>The URL(s) of the material in question.</li>
          <li>Identification of the copyrighted work you say has been infringed.</li>
          <li>Your name, address, and a contact email.</li>
          <li>
            A statement that you have a good-faith belief the use is not authorised by the
            rights-holder, its agent, or the law.
          </li>
          <li>
            A statement that the information in your notice is accurate and that you are the
            rights-holder or authorised to act on their behalf, together with your signature
            (electronic is fine).
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We acknowledge notices within 5 business days and remove or disable material that is
          clearly infringing while we look into it. If you believe your material was removed in
          error, send a counter-notice to the same address and we will reinstate it if the claim
          does not hold up. These terms are governed by the laws of the Netherlands, consistent
          with our <a href="/terms/">terms of service</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Licensing, attribution, or permission questions:
          <a href="mailto:hello@caslonmedia.com?subject=Licensing+inquiry">hello@caslonmedia.com</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    padding-block: var(--spacing-section);
  }

  .legal-page__header {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    padding-bottom: 2rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .legal-page__header h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: var(--text-display-xl);
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--color-ink-900);
    margin: 0.5rem 0 0;
  }

  .legal-page__updated {
    color: var(--color-ink-500);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }

  .prose h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.375rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--color-ink-900);
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .prose p,
  .prose ul,
  .prose ol {
    color: var(--color-ink-700);
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .prose ul {
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
  }

  .prose li {
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .prose a {
    color: var(--color-link);
    text-decoration-line: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .prose a:hover {
    color: var(--color-link-hover);
  }
</style>
